  "description": "A boarding-pass mockup printing the flight date as day+month with no year at all (\"17SEP\") came back with departureDate completely unresolved. Root cause: parseFreeTextDate required an explicit year and rejected everything else, even though resolveBcbpJulianDate already had to solve the exact same yearless-date problem for BCBP barcodes. Fixed by adding the same nearest-year inference to free-text dates. Route/destination also came back empty on this same report (the ticket prints city names \"MOSCOW\"/\"NEW YORK\", not IATA codes) - that's a separate, still-open gap (airportLookup.ts only maps 3-letter codes, not city names), not asserted here since it isn't fixed yet.",
